<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <Version>0.9.0</Version>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>true</EnforceCodeStyleInBuild>
    <AnalysisLevel>latest-all</AnalysisLevel>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      D-M2-11(a) requires that a concurrent first-use resolution of a `Login` token source be
      single-flighted, and D-M2-11(c) re-opened CFG-070 onto the traceability baseline so that
      invariant is asserted under real concurrency rather than by inspection. The `Login` variant's
      public factory lands with its credential types in M2b (D-M2-6), so the only way to drive the
      single-flight cell in M2a is `TokenSource.LoginWith`, which takes the login performer
      directly. Exposing internals to the test assembly is narrower than either shipping a public
      factory that throws (a stub — D-M1c-25 forbids it) or leaving the ruling unasserted until the
      slice that uses it (which is what D-M2-11 blocked revision 3 for).

      This changes no public surface: InternalsVisibleTo does not appear in PublicApiSurface.txt
      (CNF-027).
    -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="BastionVault.IntegrationSdk.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!--
    CNF-027 (public API baseline) was enforced by Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.PublicApiAnalyzers
    (RS0016/RS0017) through M1b, but D-M1b-19 found that enforcement was inert: AnalysisLevel
    latest-all imports Microsoft.CodeAnalysis.NetAnalyzers.props, which reassigns
    $(CodeAnalysisRuleIds) and drops the RS00xx set the analyzer relies on (confirmed with
    `dotnet build -v:diag`; also overrides the analyzer's own
    _CodeAnalysisTreatWarningsAsErrors target). A seeded new public member built with 0
    warnings and 0 errors. Setting dotnet_diagnostic.RS0016.severity=error in .editorconfig
    does not revive it. The analyzer package, and PublicAPI.Shipped.txt/PublicAPI.Unshipped.txt,
    are therefore removed rather than kept as a gate that looks green and is not.

    CNF-027 is now enforced by BastionVault.IntegrationSdk.Tests/ApiSurface/PublicApiSurfaceTests.cs,
    a reflection-based diff against the committed PublicApiSurface.txt — the same category of
    check Rust (`cargo public-api`) and Python (tests/test_api_surface.py) already run. It
    executes inside plain `dotnet test`, so no separate CI step is needed; see
    .github/workflows/dotnet.yml. The gate was proven by seeding a violation (a new public
    member) and confirming the test fails with that member named in the diff, then reverting
    the seed — see the M1b delegation report for the verbatim failure.
  -->

</Project>
